                    .column.is-8.is-offset-1-desktop
                        .project-details__intro-text-wrapper
                            %p
                                A proposal to Badia built around their tagline "El Alma de la Cocina" (the soul of the kitchen), aimed at extending the brand's strong presence in Puerto Rican households beyond the grocery aisle and into the moments, traditions, and celebrations people build around food.
                            %p
                                We developed two creative routes that both grew out of "El Alma de la Cocina" but took the brand in different directions, giving Badia flexible platforms that could carry their messaging year round and flex across key consumption seasons.
                            %p
                                The first, "Métele Sazón" (add the seasoning), was the option with attitude. A disruptive route that invites people to enjoy their food with real Boricua flavor, built on the idea that the soul of flavor always starts with the sazón. It's short, memorable, and made to live beyond a single campaign, the kind of phrase people repeat, adapt, and make their own all year, from billboards to wobblers to digital and point-of-purchase moments. It also flexes easily by season and dish, like "Métele Sazón al Pavo" around the holidays, all while reinforcing Badia as "El Alma de la Cocina."
                            %p 
                                The second, "El Sabor Nos Une" (the flavor that unites us), was the emotional option. A tribute to the power of food and spices to strengthen relationships and create new memories, and the role Badia plays in carrying on the soul of every family's recipes on. This route positions Badia as more than seasoning, but ras the flavor that shows up in the moments we share around the table. It lives naturally under "El Alma de la Cocina," elevating the tagline into a warmer, more human platform that celebrates everything from family recipes to new traditions being formed.
        .project-details__gallery-wrapper
            .project-details__discover-wrapper
                .container
                    .columns.is-variable.is-6
                        .column.is-4
                            %p.eyebrow Discover
                            %h2 The Brief
                        .column.is-8
                            %p.projects__middle-text
                                Badia came to us with a clear starting point: their sazón completa and small seasoning packets, were their top sellers, their audience spanned adults in their 20s through 50s, and they wanted their tagline, "El Alma de la Cocina," to become more than a line on the label. Beyond that, the brief was open, which meant the direction of the campaign was ours to shape.
