                    .columns.is-variable.is-6
                        .column.is-4
                            %p.eyebrow Strategy
                            %h2 Retail
                        .column.is-8
                            %p.projects__middle-text
                                Dominating the point of sale was the goal: interactive displays and POP materials designed with the campaign's vibrant new palette to stop traffic in the aisle and make Badia the first choice on the shelf. Positioned right at the shelf, the wobblers used quick, attention-grabbing copy pulled from both routes to catch someone's eye mid-aisle. One of the display stands took that idea further, organizing spices by row into collections built around arroz con pollo, camarones al ajillo, sancocho, and carne guisada, each with a QR code linking to the recipe. Instead of asking shoppers to already know what they needed, the display did the thinking for them, turning a routine grocery trip into a small moment of "El Alma de la Cocina" in action.
