            .project-details__description-wrapper
                .container
                    .columns.is-variable.is-6
                        .column.is-4
                            %p.eyebrow Strategy
                            %h2 Experiences
                        .column.is-8
                            %p.projects__middle-text
                                The food truck took the campaign on the road as the Métele Sazón Tour, tagged #NoSoySoso, giving people a chance to experience Badia in person instead of just seeing it on a shelf or a billboard. At each stop, Chef Edgardo Noel prepared dishes using different Badia spice blends, showing how the same recipe could change completely depending on which mix went into it. A second station, the Flavor Bar, let people get hands-on: smelling, tasting, and combining spices themselves while getting recommendations on what to use. As an extra layer, each stop could include a "Sazónómetro," where people tried a dish and voted on how it landed, from "le falta sazón" (needs more seasoning) to "¡se botó!" (it's amazing), turning the activation into something people participate in.
            .project-details__gallery-wrapper
                .container
                    = image_tag "https://nicolada-website.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/badia-food-truck.webp", loading: 'lazy'
            .project-details__description-wrapper
                .container
                    .columns.is-variable.is-6
                        .column.is-4
                            %p.eyebrow Strategy
                            %h2 Digital
                        .column.is-8
                            %p.projects__middle-text
                                Online, the goal was sazón digital, taking the concept from the screen to the table. We amplified the year-round platform by connecting Badia's communities through dynamic content and promotional pages built around key seasons, giving both creative routes a consistent home to live in beyond the physical world.
                            %br
                            %p.projects__middle-text
                                The visual direction leaned bold and pop art inspired: saturated solid-color backgrounds, close-up shots of food that made every dish feel irresistible, and bold typography paired with playful color to give Badia an identity that felt more appetizing and memorable than a typical spice brand's feed. Alongside the food itself, the content made room for the people around it, family moments where food does the connecting, plus recipes that gave followers a reason to keep coming back to the page.
